+## 2v2 with the other fight drawn (docs/camera/pending/others-frame): the other fights' standing bodies join the one view by
+## the one-versus-many rule (docs/camera/one-v-many.md section 3). Each counts by a weight that moves MANY_RATE a tick (a join or a
+## leave takes 40 ticks and steps nothing): 1 while the zoom that fits him with the pair (and the nearer others) stays above
+## OTHERS_ZKEEP of the pair's own and OTHERS_R_MIN of the height a body, 0 past MANY_JOIN of that limit. So a pair nearby makes a wider shot of
+## all four, and one farther off is let go, eased, leaving the frame to this pair. The focus leans toward the set's centre by at most
+## MANY_PULL of the width. A body that's out, higher than MANY_UP_BH over the pair or deeper than MANY_DEPTH counts for nothing.
+## Weights are keyed by fight and place; a key that's gone (the fight held changed) is forgotten.
+func _others_set(S: SimState, mx: float, ahead: float, dy: float, y_mid: float) -> Dictionary:
+	var pair: Array = S.fighters.slice(0, 2)
+	var A = pair[0]
+	var B = pair[1]
+	var r1: float = SimWrap.sdx(A.x, B.x)
+	var lo: float = minf(0.0, r1)
+	var hi: float = maxf(0.0, r1)
+	var y_lo: float = minf(float(A.y), float(B.y))
